# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here has a value on purpose:
# committing an example with a working default is how a secret or an unintended
# model choice ends up in the repo.

# The provider credential. Read at OpenAIChatClient construction; a missing or
# blank value raises ProviderAuthError before any request is attempted.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# The chat model to call. Deliberately has NO built-in default: this project
# does not choose a model for you, so any Chat Completions-compatible model your
# account can call is a valid choice. A missing or blank value raises
# ClientConfigurationError -- a local configuration mistake, not the provider
# rejecting anything.
#
# Whatever you put here also needs a reviewed row in llm/pricing.py MODEL_RATES,
# or cost estimation raises UnknownModelRateError rather than guessing a price.
OPENAI_MODEL=

# The model's real, published context window, in tokens. Required, with no
# default -- the same argument LLMGateway.context_window makes: a default
# would be one model's number silently applied to whichever model you set
# above. For gpt-4o this is 128000; look up whatever you chose.
OPENAI_CONTEXT_WINDOW=

# The embedding model retrieval uses. Read by OpenAIEmbeddingsClient at
# construction; a missing or blank value raises ClientConfigurationError, the
# same way OPENAI_MODEL does, and for a stronger reason: the choice is baked
# into every stored vector. A collection embedded with one model cannot be
# searched with another, so changing this later means re-embedding the corpus.
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

# Where Qdrant is. Started by docker-compose.yml; leave blank to use the
# compose default of http://localhost:6333. Not a secret, and not required --
# it has a constructor default for the same reason the chat base URL does.
QDRANT_URL=

# The Qdrant API key. A local Qdrant started by the compose file has no
# authentication, so this is normally blank; a hosted one needs it.
QDRANT_API_KEY=

# Which collection the chunks live in. Blank uses the default. Worth setting
# per embedding model in a shared deployment: vectors are only comparable to
# vectors made by the same model, and ingestion refuses to write into a
# collection of a different width rather than mixing them.
QDRANT_COLLECTION=

# Which collection the memory index lives in. Blank uses the default,
# `project_memories`. A separate variable from QDRANT_COLLECTION on purpose:
# pointing the corpus somewhere else and pointing memory somewhere else are
# different decisions, and one variable serving both would make the second
# happen by accident whenever somebody made the first.
#
# This collection is an index, not a store. The memories table in Postgres is
# the record, so rebuilding this collection loses nothing.
QDRANT_MEMORY_COLLECTION=

# Where Postgres is -- the evidence store for runs, trace events, audit rows,
# model-call telemetry and pending approvals. Started by docker-compose.yml;
# leave blank to use the compose default of
# postgresql://agentic_erp:agentic_erp@localhost:5432/agentic_erp. Not a
# secret while the compose file's throwaway credentials are what you run; a
# hosted database replaces the whole URL with real credentials.
#
# The schema does not create itself: run `uv run python scripts/init_postgres.py`
# once after the container is up. Connection problems surface as
# StoreConnectionError at connect, not mid-request.
POSTGRES_URL=

# Where the *test* database is -- the one `uv run pytest -m postgres` is
# allowed to TRUNCATE. Read only by tests/persistence/conftest.py and
# `scripts/init_postgres.py --test`, never by the server. Leave blank to use
# the compose default of
# postgresql://agentic_erp:agentic_erp@localhost:5432/agentic_erp_test --
# same server, same credential as POSTGRES_URL, different database. Whatever
# you set here MUST name a database ending in `_test`:
# assert_test_database refuses anything else before opening a connection, so
# a copy-pasted POSTGRES_URL here fails loudly instead of truncating the
# evidence store a running server writes to (ADR 0018).
POSTGRES_TEST_URL=

# Whether consolidation proposes memories to write at all. "off" disables the
# LLMMemoryProposer model call; anything else, including unset, keeps it on.
# Recall and the intent operations are unaffected either way. A deployment
# turns this off while deciding whether the extra model call is worth its
# cost.
MEMORY_PROPOSER=

# Where the dev chat's actor directory is read from. Blank uses
# data/users.json -- the default cast committed to the repo.
USERS_PATH=

# -- Dev toggles -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read only by composition/settings.py, logged loudly at startup, and never
# referenced by engine/tools/rag code directly. They exist because the
# registry's real budgets (30 reads/60s, an eight-step turn, a six-turn
# window) are none of them things a person clicking around a browser demo can
# exhaust in a reasonable session -- a scripted test reaches the same paths
# with a fake clock and a tight fixture instead. Leave all of these blank for
# a normal run.

# "N/S" (calls/seconds), e.g. "2/20" -- overrides every read tool's rate
# limit so T10 in docs/manual-test.md is reachable by hand. Writes keep their
# own budget regardless; see tools/registry.py.
# DEV_TOOL_RATE_LIMIT=

# "1" offers get_project_status_flaky to the planner instead of
# get_project_status, so the retry-then-succeed path (T11) is reachable
# without a scripted fake.
# DEV_FLAKY_STATUS=

# An integer step budget, overriding engine/workflow.py's MAX_STEPS (8), so
# the max_steps_exceeded failure (G1) is reachable in a short conversation.
# DEV_MAX_STEPS=

# An integer turn count, overriding context/history_injection.py's
# HISTORY_TURN_LIMIT (6), so short-term-memory eviction (M8) is reachable
# without six real turns.
# DEV_HISTORY_TURN_LIMIT=

# "1" streams a turn's model calls' prompt and reply text to the trace panel
# live (docs/trace-inspector-plan.md) -- a different shape of toggle from the
# others above: it does not loosen a budget, it turns on a capability that
# repeats evidence/history/memory text on every model call and is expensive
# to leave on by default. Never persisted regardless of this setting.
# DEV_TRACE_MODEL_IO=
